@page "/data/versioning"
@inject NavigationManager NavigationManager

<PageTitle>Manage Data Versions</PageTitle>

<MudContainer MaxWidth="MaxWidth.ExtraLarge" Class="pa-4">

    <MudStack Row="true" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Justify="Justify.SpaceBetween" Class="mb-4">
        <MudStack Spacing="0">
            <MudText Typo="Typo.h5">Manage Data Versions</MudText>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Color="Color.Secondary">Snapshots of PPDM39 tables, and who changed what</MudText>
        </MudStack>
        <MudButton Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                   StartIcon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Security"
                   OnClick='() => NavigationManager.NavigateTo("/data/audit")'>
            View Access Audit
        </MudButton>
    </MudStack>

    @* No table snapshots in the API (2026-10-10): the versioning service keeps versions of one record at a time, and nothing
       captures a whole table's rows as a snapshot. "New Snapshot" sent the table's name as the record to version and failed
       with a server error every time, and the history listed versions that could not exist, each version number shown as a
       row count. Both endpoints answer that they are not available, and the page no longer offers them. *@
    <MudAlert Severity="Severity.Info">
        Taking and listing snapshots of a table is not available yet.
    </MudAlert>

</MudContainer>
